    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0431" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/585: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-23T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                                1920—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 24—4:03
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Minister for Foreign Affairs made reply last night to Bolivian note of March
                        16,<anchor n="85" xml:id="d348-f1"/> reaffirming position of Peru. He stated
                    to me that this was the last reply he was sending to Bolivia as there was
                    nothing more to be said by Peru. All agitation has ceased and perfect calm
                    prevails in Peru.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d348-f1" n="85" xml:id="d348-f1-content">
                <p>Bolivian note of Mar. 16 was in reply to the Peruvian counter-reply of Mar. 6
                    referred to in the Chargé’s telegram no. 46, Mar. 5, <ref target="#pg328">p.
                        328</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
